      "message": "Thanks. Yeah, the instruction output is a little baroque. I tried to make it easier to read than a raw assembly dump, but there are still quirks for sure. $123 is a value on the stack, in position 123. $123..125 is three values on the stack (in positions 123, 124, and 125). Most ops should hopefully be somewhat self-explanatory ($1 +\u003d $2 means, compute \"$1 + $2\" and store it in \"$1\"). The mask handling stuff is a little weird if you\u0027ve never dealt with SIMD pseudo control flow before unfortunately.",
